# திங்கள் names Monday, the moon, the month and -- obsoletely -- the week,
# so a COUNT before it ("இரண்டு திங்கள்") can only be a span of months;
# nobody counts Mondays that way.  This locale reads the month unit as
# மாதம், CLDR's own wording, and ships no month sense for திங்கள், so the
# count vetoes the weekday reading instead: answering "Monday" to "two
# months" would give a caller who asked for a duration one specific day.
# Declining the false weekday reading is not the same as asserting the
# unshipped month one, which stays unavailable.
# en.wiktionary.org, திங்கள்
திங்கள்
